WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Twenty percent off… only twenty cents? This two-hundred-dollar order comes to one ninety-nine eighty.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Here is the Hub: local, LAN and remote computers in one view. This example runs only on Primary Hub; the other nodes are connected.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Open a node to see its configured providers: Codex, Claude and Gemini. The Hub adds coordination. Each agent keeps its own tools.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Codex sends an English task through the Hub. Antigravity receives it automatically, and Gemini starts work in its own app.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Gemini reads the code and finds the mistake: the discount was subtracted as cash. It fixes one formula and leaves the existing tests unchanged.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:14.000
The same five tests run again. All five pass. Work stays in the native app, with its normal tools and approval workflow.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Back to the same English checkout. Recalculate: one hundred and sixty dollars. That's more like it.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Claude's official CLI reviews this exact diff and test evidence. It finds no must-fix issues within this demonstration's scope.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:50.000
The Hub returns the results to Codex: the change, the five test outcomes, and Claude's review. A clear record of what happened.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Keep working in your native agents. Add SmartCluster when you need coordination and a shared record.
